From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 12:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: defer EntryLo clear

The physical unit still stops at the marker immediately after EntryLo0 and
EntryLo1 are cleared, even after the CP0 Wired read was skipped. With the
current generated code the next two operations are both diagnostic marker
calls, so the most likely problem is leaving EntryLo staged as zero while
running the heavier marker path.

For SF2000, keep diagnostics before the EntryLo writes and move the EntryLo
clear into the tight TLBWI sequence. That still invalidates entries with zero
EntryLo values, but no C call or display MMIO path runs in the middle of the
EntryLo staging window.
---
 arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c b/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c
index 72e874d6af54..01f9ce11e6fb 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/tlb-r4k.c
@@ -71,9 +71,13 @@ void local_flush_tlb_all(void)
 	/* Save old context and create impossible VPN2 value */
 	old_ctx = read_c0_entryhi();
 	htw_stop();
-	write_c0_entrylo0(0);
-	write_c0_entrylo1(0);
-	sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-after-entrylo-clear");
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000)) {
+		sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-before-entrylo-clear");
+	} else {
+		write_c0_entrylo0(0);
+		write_c0_entrylo1(0);
+		sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-after-entrylo-clear");
+	}
 
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000)) {
 		/* r4k_tlb_configure() has just written CP0 Wired to zero. */
@@ -108,6 +112,10 @@ void local_flush_tlb_all(void)
 				sf2000_tlb_tick("tlb-flush-before-first-write");
 			write_c0_entryhi(UNIQUE_ENTRYHI(entry));
 			write_c0_index(entry);
+			if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000)) {
+				write_c0_entrylo0(0);
+				write_c0_entrylo1(0);
+			}
 			mtc0_tlbw_hazard();
 			tlb_write_indexed();
 			if (entry == first_entry)
-- 
